  'st-james-spring-still-dry-city-seeks-hydrologist-2026-11-26',
  'St James spring on Main Road is still dry and the City wants a hydrologist to find out why',
  'Utilities', '2026-11-26', 'Cape Town Etc', 'https://www.capetownetc.com/news/historic-cape-town-spring-runs-dry-no-one-knows-why/',
  'The St James spring on Main Road has stopped flowing and the City says it is securing a hydrologist to work out the cause.',
  'The free spring water collection point at St James, on Main Road near the border with Muizenberg, remains dry, and nobody has yet established why it stopped.

The City of Cape Town closed the collection point at 4 Main Road, Muizenberg, in March after a routine inspection found no water coming from the source. The City promised to look into the cause and to clean and service the site. Residents say the flow stopped in August of last year. The spring had kept running through the 2018 drought, when people queued there to fill containers.

According to a report first published by GroundUp, the City now says it has found no change since its last report and is securing a hydrologist to try to identify the cause. The City water and sanitation directorate says it has inspected the collection points and is talking to other departments, contractors and the public. Some residents suspect that paving work in the area or a shift in the underlying geology may be to blame, but this has not been confirmed.

Residents who want spring water in the meantime can use the Newlands Spring beside the Newlands pool on Main Road, which the City said was open daily from 05:00 to 21:00 when it closed St James. The City reminds users that spring water is untreated and is collected and used at their own risk.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.capetownetc.com/news/historic-cape-town-spring-runs-dry-no-one-knows-why/", "https://www.capetown.gov.za/Media-and-news/St James Spring closed for water collection"]',
  'agent'
);
